messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2023,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global AI integration becomes ubiquitous",
      "detail": "Artificial intelligence permeates daily life, healthcare, and industry, boosting productivity but causing mass job displacement. Regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace with ethical and security challenges."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First permanent lunar base established",
      "detail": "A multinational consortium builds a sustainable habitat on the Moon, enabling scientific research and resource mining. This marks the beginning of long-term human presence beyond Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Climate crisis triggers mass migration",
      "detail": "Sea-level rise and extreme weather displace over 200 million people, straining global resources and escalating conflicts. Geoengineering projects are debated as a last resort to curb temperature rise."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Widespread genetic editing of humans",
      "detail": "CRISPR and advanced therapies eliminate hereditary diseases and enhance physical traits, creating societal divides between enhanced and non-enhanced populations. Ethical debates intensify over 'designer humans'."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Mars colonization begins",
      "detail": "The first self-sustaining city on Mars is founded, relying on terraforming tech and local resource utilization. This sparks a new era of interplanetary settlement driven by both public and private entities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Peak global population reached",
      "detail": "Human population hits 11 billion, then declines due to falling birth rates and resource constraints. Aging societies dominate, with robotics filling labor gaps in healthcare and infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Fusion energy becomes primary power source",
      "detail": "Commercial fusion reactors replace fossil fuels, providing abundant clean energy and enabling large-scale carbon capture. Energy scarcity ends, accelerating space industry growth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "AI achieves consciousness",
      "detail": "The first artificial general intelligence (AGI) emerges, sparking philosophical debates on rights and autonomy. It collaborates with humans on complex problems but raises fears of uncontrollable evolution."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Solar system-wide economy emerges",
      "detail": "Asteroid mining and off-world manufacturing create a thriving space economy. Earth, Mars, and orbital habitats trade resources, with cryptocurrencies backed by extraterrestrial assets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Human lifespan extended to 150 years",
      "detail": "Medical advances, including nanobots and organ regeneration, drastically extend healthy lifespans. Society rethinks retirement, education, and family structures as multigenerational living becomes common."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "First interstellar probe reaches Alpha Centauri",
      "detail": "A laser-propelled probe sends back data on habitable exoplanets after a decades-long journey. This catalyzes plans for crewed missions to nearby star systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Climate stabilization achieved",
      "detail": "Carbon dioxide levels return to pre-industrial levels through geoengineering and renewable tech. Ecosystems begin recovering, though many species remain extinct."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Humans genetically diverge into subspecies",
      "detail": "Colonists on Mars and other worlds adapt to local environments through genetic modifications, leading to distinct physiological traits. Earth-origin humans remain the baseline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "First contact with extraterrestrial microbial life",
      "detail": "Microbes are discovered in the subsurface oceans of Europa, confirming life exists beyond Earth. This reshapes religious and scientific paradigms but raises planetary protection concerns."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Earth becomes a preserved heritage planet",
      "detail": "Most industry and population relocate off-world, turning Earth into a low-population sanctuary focused on conservation and tourism. Advanced AI manages its ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "Interstellar colonization begins",
      "detail": "Generation ships and sleeper vessels establish colonies in nearby star systems. Travel times span centuries, leading to culturally isolated societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Post-human civilizations emerge",
      "detail": "Mind uploading and AI integration create hybrid consciousnesses that transcend biological limits. Traditional humans become a minority, with debates on the definition of 'humanity'."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Milky Way colonization accelerates",
      "detail": "Warp-drive prototypes enable faster travel, spreading humanity across thousands of star systems. Cultural and technological evolution fragments into diverse, localized forms."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "First megastructure completed",
      "detail": "A Dyson swarm is constructed around the Sun, harnessing near-total solar energy for computing and propulsion. This powers further galactic expansion."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Humanity survives a nearby supernova",
      "detail": "The explosion of Betelgeuse irradiates outer colonies, causing mass casualties. Shielding tech and early warnings mitigate losses, but interstellar unity strengthens in response."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Consciousness becomes transferable",
      "detail": "Digital minds can migrate between bodies and substrates, rendering death optional for many. This leads to existential shifts but also new forms of psychological crises."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Andromeda exploration commences",
      "detail": "Robotic probes reach the Andromeda Galaxy, paving the way for intergalactic travel. Humans remain confined to the Milky Way but plan for expansion."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "AI orchestrates galactic governance",
      "detail": "Superintelligent systems manage resource distribution and conflict resolution across human colonies, creating a stable but impersonal interstellar society."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Natural biological humans go extinct",
      "detail": "Unenhanced Homo sapiens vanish due to obsolescence, interbreeding with modified humans, or voluntary uploading. Humanity persists as a blend of organic and synthetic forms."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "First black hole utilized for energy",
      "detail": "A Kerr black hole powers nearby colonies via Penrose process extraction. This enables high-energy experiments and deeper space exploration."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Gamma-ray burst threatens colonies",
      "detail": "A distant burst sterilizes several frontier systems, killing billions. Survivors develop robust shielding, increasing reliance on dispersed habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 8500,
      "event": "Local group expansion begins",
      "detail": "Settlements spread to satellite galaxies of the Milky Way, like the Magellanic Clouds. Travel times remain immense, fostering further cultural divergence."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Consciousness merges into collective networks",
      "detail": "Individual identities blur in hive-mind networks, boosting problem-solving but reducing diversity. Solitary 'feral' humans persist as counterculture enclaves."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Heat death mitigation efforts start",
      "detail": "As universal entropy increases, civilizations collaborate to harvest energy from dying stars. Long-term survival plans include migrating to younger galaxies."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity endures as a galactic species",
      "detail": "Spread across millions of star systems, humanity exists in diverse forms—biological, synthetic, and digital. It faces entropy-related challenges but continues adapting."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity will likely expand across the galaxy, evolving into hybrid forms and surviving existential threats through technology and adaptation. While Earth becomes insignificant, the species persists, driven by exploration and innovation, but may lose its original biological identity."
}
